WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Phases of a Successful Six Sigma Roll Out

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.966
Welcome to this session on deployment planning and focus on the word deployment.

3
00:00:12.966 --> 00:00:15.966
Now, what do I mean by deployment?

4
00:00:15.966 --> 00:00:20.066
Well, earlier we had talked about the idea of deployment

5
00:00:20.066 --> 00:00:26.599
and contrasted that to the idea of implementation.

6
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:31.500
And we also looked at the idea of application.

7
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:35.500
Now, there's three different words there because there's three different concepts.

8
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:39.133
A lot of people like to try to mix them.  But, in my way of thinking

9
00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:43.966
deployment is different than implementation, different than application.

10
00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:50.732
Let me use a military example. I deploy troops on the battlefield.

11
00:00:50.733 --> 00:00:54.199
You're going out to fight defects, to fight variation.

12
00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.466
You're sending black belt troops, green belt troops, white belt troops.

13
00:00:57.466 --> 00:01:00.766
You gotta deploy them on the battlefield.

14
00:01:00.766 --> 00:01:04.866
That's what the leadership of the corporation does. They are responsible for

15
00:01:04.866 --> 00:01:10.166
deploying people and knowledge, and resources. Spreading it out.

16
00:01:10.166 --> 00:01:13.199
Rolling it out.

17
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.233
To all the different business units and departments and every

18
00:01:16.233 --> 00:01:20.233
crook and cranny or whatever you call it, through the whole organization.

19
00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:24.233
Then they,  the black belts, the green belts, the white belts, they implement

20
00:01:24.233 --> 00:01:28.866
the principles of Six Sigma.

21
00:01:28.866 --> 00:01:32.866
They do that by applying the tools of Six Sigma.

22
00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:37.766
So just like soldiers. A general deploys troops on the battlefield.

23
00:01:37.766 --> 00:01:41.466
The majors and colonels implement.

24
00:01:41.466 --> 00:01:46.766
And lieutenants, sergeants, and everyone else, apply the tools of warfare.

25
00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:52.499
So, we have to have deployment plans, implementation plans, and application plans.

26
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.833
Those are all vital planning elements as we move forward with rolling out Six Sigma.

27
00:01:58.833 --> 00:02:02.833
So when you hear somebody say, how do you roll out Six Sigma?

28
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:08.266
Well, we do it by having deployment plans, implementation plans, and application plans.

29
00:02:08.266 --> 00:02:11.899
And that forms right, pretty much, in parallel

30
00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.900
with the classic triangle we been talking about, about BOP.

31
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:22.766
Business level deployment. Operations level implementation. Process level application.

32
00:02:22.766 --> 00:02:27.266
So, that's what we mean when we start talking about deployment planning.

33
00:02:27.266 --> 00:02:33.566
That word deployment is a more global word that encompasses several things.

34
00:02:33.566 --> 00:02:38.566
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
